Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 16 02:37:30 2026 +0000

    Retry data stores whose provisioning gave up, every ten minutes
    
    A store whose provisioning gave up (five tries over about half an hour,
    say through a database outage) stayed failed until the next deploy's
    migrate_all, while the API and UI told the user "We'll try again". So
    did a store whose provisioning task was never queued. The provisioning
    worker now runs a beat (-B) that tries those stores again every ten
    minutes. A store made within the last hour is left to its own task.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KC3fucdE9rANvvSzGLn7e5

